2.7pt'><\/td>\r\n  <td width=90 valign=top style='width:67.5pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'><\/td>\r\n  <td width=252 valign=top style='width:189.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'><\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr style='height:14.85pt'>\r\n  <td width=317 valign=top style='width:238.1pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:14.85pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\r\n  \"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=108 valign=top style='width:81.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:14.85pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=90 valign=top style='width:67.5pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:14.85pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=252 valign=top style='width:189.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:14.85pt'><\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n<\/table>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:-18.0pt'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-left:-18.0pt'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>COMMENT<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:-74.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:-18.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u00a0<\/span><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Tissue&nbsp;transglutaminase&nbsp;antibody&nbsp;(tTG),&nbsp;IgA&nbsp;class&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;the&nbsp;primary&nbsp;test&nbsp;ordered&nbsp;to&nbsp;screen&nbsp;for&nbsp;celiac&nbsp;disease.&nbsp;It&nbsp;is&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;sensitive&nbsp;and&nbsp;specific&nbsp;blood&nbsp;test&nbsp;for&nbsp;celiac&nbsp;disease\r\nand is the single test preferred by the American College of Gastroenterology,\r\naccording to its 2013 guidelines, as well as the American Gastroenterology\r\nAssociation for the detection of celiac disease in those over the age of 2\r\nyears. Tissue transglutaminase is one of the main endomysial autoantigens that\r\ncan be easily detected for the diagnosis of Celiac disease. Other recommended\r\ntests are Endomysial, Gliadin &amp; Reticulin antibodies along with small\r\nintestinal biopsy. Negative serology does not exclude a diagnosis of GSE. IgA\r\ndeficiency should be considered in patients with suggestive clinical\r\npresentation. The IgG class of anti-tTG may be ordered as an alternative in\r\nthose who have a deficiency of IgA. If the anti-tTG, IgA or IgG test is\r\npositive, then the test can also be used to monitor a person with celiac\r\ndisease and to help evaluate the effectiveness of treatment; antibody levels\r\nshould fall when gluten is removed from the diet.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:-74.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:-18.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><b><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>NOTE<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:-74.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:-18.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u00a01. To diagnose Celiac disease\r\nthe test should be performed before eliminating gluten from the diet. <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:-74.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:-18.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>2. False positive results are\r\nseen in Type 1 Diabetes, Chronic Liver Disease, Heart Failure and Psoriatic or\r\nRheumatoid Arthritis. It is likely that proteins other than tTG may act as\r\nantigens for anti-tTG antibodies. <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:-74.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:-18.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>3. False negative results may be\r\nseen in children below 2 years &amp; patients with IgA deficiency. There is\r\nhigh prevalence of IgA deficiency in Celiac disease thus simultaneous screening\r\nfor IgA level has been recommended. <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:-74.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:-18.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>4. A useful test for exclusion of\r\nCeliac disease is HLA - DNA testing for the presence of DQ2 and DQ8. <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0cm;margin-right:-74.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:-18.0pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>5.After several weeks on gluten\r\nfree diet,t-Tg antibody levels may become normal.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<\/div>","page":{"size":"612.0pt 792.0pt","margin":"148.85pt 90.0pt 72.0pt 42.55pt"}}